    "result": "I implemented `parse_line(line, sep=\",\")` in `solution.py` following `spec.md`, and wrote 46 pytest tests in `tests/test_solution.py` covering unquoted and quoted fields, doubled quotes, embedded separators and newlines, and every error case in the spec. The implementation scans the line once: a field that starts with `\"` is read until its undoubled closing quote, and the character after that quote must be the separator or end of line. An unquoted field is read up to the next separator and rejects `\"`, `\\r` and `\\n`. Type checks run first, then separator validation. Running `python -m pytest -q tests` gave 46 passed. I did not install anything or create files outside `solution.py` and `tests/`.",
